# Keyword exceptions for the image build. Keep empty if possible — stable amd64 only.
media-libs/libva-intel-media-driver ~amd64  # no stable amd64 ebuild in tree at this snapshot
x11-drivers/nvidia-drivers           ~amd64  # no stable amd64 ebuild in tree at this snapshot

# The ONLY ~amd64 package in the desktop set, and a deliberate departure from the rule in the
# line above — recorded here rather than slipped in. Plasma Login Manager shipped with Plasma
# 6.6 as KDE's SDDM replacement and has no stable ebuild yet; x11-misc/sddm does
# (0.21.0_p20250502-r1), so this exception is the price of choosing PLM (plan/09). It is worth
# paying because PLM reuses kwin as its greeter compositor rather than starting a second one,
# which matters in an image that is Wayland-only by construction.
#
# Pinned to =6.6.6 deliberately, not left open: both 6.6.6-r1 and 6.7.4-r1 raise QTMIN to
# >=6.11.2, which is itself ~amd64 and would pull a ~amd64 Qt AND the ~amd64 Plasma 6.7.4 set
# in behind it. 6.6.6 needs only QTMIN=6.10.0, satisfied by the stable dev-qt/qtbase-6.11.1.
# One ~amd64 package, not a hundred.
# Drop the pin — not the entry — when 6.7.x stabilises alongside the rest of Plasma.
=kde-plasma/plasma-login-manager-6.6.6   ~amd64

# Everything else in @desktop is stable amd64 at the pinned snapshot, verified against the
